#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amarok&nbsp;2 sports a three-pane interface by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "The left pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "To the left, we have..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left pane is tabbed and retractable. The first tab is the "
"<guilabel>collection browser</guilabel>, which is the primary interface to "
"your local collection. Attached devices will also show up here. There is a "
"tab for all <guilabel>Internet services</guilabel> that you have enabled. "
"Here, you can browse listings of radio stations and podcasts; listen/"
"subscribe to them, interact with your <ulink url=\"http://www.last.fm\">last."
"fm</ulink> account, purchase music from online stores such as Magnatune and "
"download independent artists' music from Jamendo and more. The "
"<guilabel>Playlist</guilabel> tab allows you to create and manage dynamic "
"and traditional playlists and podcasts. Finally, the <guilabel>Files</"
"guilabel> tab displays an integrated file browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "The central pane (Context View)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the middle..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where all the action is. The pane contains applets that dynamically "
"change to display context information about the song that is currently "
"playing. You can see the rating, score and play count of the currently "
"playing song, other songs by the same artist that you have, the lyrics of "
"the song, the <ulink url=\"http://www.wikipedia.org\">Wikipedia</ulink> page "
"on the artist and more. These applets can be added, removed or rearranged "
"using the <guilabel>applet bar</guilabel> at the bottom of the pane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "The right pane (Playlist View)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "And on the right..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Amarok&nbsp;2 has the most configurable play list of any music player in "
"existence. While most offer a columnar layout as default and perhaps a few "
"other fixed views for the play list, Amarok&nbsp;2 puts the power in your "
"hands to shape the play list any way you see fit. To start you off, there "
"are three example play list layouts that you can use as starting points to "
"create the layout that fits your flow the best."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:100
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "music"
msgid "Plays music"
msgstr "តន្ត្រី​"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Amarok&nbsp;2 can support most popular formats for music files. The actual "
"list of formats is dependent on the codecs and audio backend in use on your "
"system. There's also support for traditional play lists &mdash; you can "
"create, save and load all the play lists you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Device Support"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently, basic iPod, MTP and UMS device support are enabled if the "
"required packages are installed. This will be improved upon and more devices "
"will be supported in the future releases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button <guilabel>Toggle Unified View Mode</guilabel> at the top of the "
"collection lets you merge collections. This means songs from your local "
"collection, audio CD, mp3-player and so on will be shown in one unified "
"collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configurable Context View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Context view</guilabel>, the centerpiece attraction in "
"Amarok&nbsp;2, can automatically fetch contextual information about the "
"currently playing song (such as album art, lyrics or <ulink url=\"http://www."
"wikipedia.org\">Wikipedia</ulink> information) from the Internet and display "
"them. This is one of the unique features of the Amarok series."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "More Internet Services"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some Internet services shown on the left pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Amarok&nbsp;2 opens the gateway to a rich multimedia experience on the "
"Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sporting interfaces to services such as Ampache music servers and mp3tunes "
"lockers, it allows you to listen to your music from anywhere in the world."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can sample and buy music from Magnatune."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the Jamendo service, you can listen to and download music from "
"independent artists who you can support with your donations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With integrated <ulink url=\"http://www.last.fm\">last.fm</ulink> "
"functionality, you can scrobble your tracks, use <ulink url=\"http://www."
"last.fm\">last.fm</ulink> features like statistics, charts and listen to "
"radio streams customized to your music taste &mdash; all from Amarok&nbsp;2."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And that is just the beginning &mdash; you can add even more Internet "
"services using the <guilabel>Script Manager</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Script Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Scripts are add-ons that allow you to extend Amarok&nbsp;2&rsquo;s "
"functionality in innovative ways. Using the <guilabel>Script Manager</"
"guilabel>, you can manage these scripts in that it allows you to install/"
"remove or enable/disable scripts you already have. You can also use the "
"<guilabel>Get More Scripts</guilabel> feature to download new scripts "
"submitted by other users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cover Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can browse through your music collection using the nifty cover manager "
"that displays the album art."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rating and scoring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can show your love for the songs by rating them. Amarok&nbsp;2 supports "
"&frac12;&sdot;&#10025; ratings, too. In addition, Amarok&nbsp;2 can "
"calculate a score (a sort of guessed rating) depending on metrics such as "
"how often you listen to or skip a song."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pop-Up Dropper"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is an innovative interface that offers contextual options (such as the "
"ones you see in a <guilabel>right-click menu</guilabel>) that you can "
"<quote>drop</quote> a song into. Grab a song and see it appear in the "
"context view pane!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configurable Playlist View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The currently loaded play list is highly configurable and can show "
"information about the songs in any form you like. If you are used to the "
"<guilabel>Spreadsheet View</guilabel> found in Amarok&nbsp;1.x series and "
"other music players, you can have that, too! The <guilabel>Playlist View</"
"guilabel> also allows you to save or export the current playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic Playlists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "A little bit of this, a little bit of that&hellip;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Amarok&nbsp;2 allows you to create weighted random play lists that adhere to "
"various criteria exactly (<emphasis>Proportional bias</emphasis>) or "
"approximately (<emphasis>Fuzzy bias</emphasis>). For example, you can create "
"a play list that will be randomly populated by songs that are rated more "
"than 3 stars and are approximately from around the year 1967!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replay Gain Support"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Amarok&nbsp;2 supports replay gain tag information embedded in files and "
"automatically adjusts the overall volume of the song to a common level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rediscover your music!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hints, Tips and FAQs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you find that most of your music is recognized by Amarok, but some "
"folders are not properly picked up, open console and type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "touch <replaceable>folder</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"where <replaceable>folder</replaceable> is the path to the folder that has "
"the problem. Then select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Amarok</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in Amarok "
"main window menu, and open <menuchoice><guimenu>Collection</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Rescan Collection</guimenuitem></menuchoice> page. Your "
"folder should be visible again now."
msgstr ""

